{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_018Eywjb6ZL3pnjA3iBt5rzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- `anchor_gui.py` is the Anchor GUI: a local web-based dashboard that starts a local HTTP server (stdlib `http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer`) serving an interactive dashboard with full read/write access, exposing API endpoints so every click writes directly to the markdown files, logs changes, and refreshes state.\n- It runs with `python3 anchor_gui.py` (default browser) or `--port 8777`, and uses Python stdlib only (`json, logging, os, re, socket, sys, threading, time, traceback, webbrowser`, `http.server`, `urllib.parse`).\n- Data paths resolve through the shared `paths` helper (`ANCHOR_DIR`, `DASHBOARD_MD`, `PROJECTS_MD`, `INBOX_MD`, `DOMAINS_DIR`, `LOGS_DIR`, `CANCELLED_MD`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER_MD`), honoring the `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR` env var, with a process-wide `WRITE_LOCK` held around every markdown/JSON mutation so concurrent requests cannot lose an update.\n- A `BUILD_ID` cache-bust identity is computed once at startup from `git rev-parse --short HEAD` (falling back to source-file mtime), and a self-healing client JS template (`_CACHE_BUST_JS_TEMPLATE`) unregisters leftover service workers and clears stale Cache Storage on redeploy.\n- Markdown parsing/gathering is provided by `parse_tasks_from_md`, `serialize_task_line`, `parse_projects_from_md`, `parse_inbox_from_md`, `parse_archived_tasks`, and `gather_all` (which deduplicates tasks).\n- It implements a hand-rolled stdlib WebSocket codec for the terminal subsystem â€” `ws_accept_key`, `encode_text_frame`, `encode_close_frame`, `encode_pong_frame`, `_encode_frame`, and `decode_frames`.\n- Static-asset routes are traversal-guarded via `_unsafe_path_seg`, serving `anchor_term_asset`, `xterm_asset`, and `brand_asset` (Ghost World Labs brand mark).\n- R&D project lifecycle helpers include `open_project_instance`/`close_project_instance`, best-effort bootstrap (`_maybe_git_init`, `_bootstrap_project_best_effort`), `create_new_folder_project`, `select_existing_project`, and `discover_and_adopt`.\n- Background summary/handoff triggers are present: `_trigger_project_summary`, `_trigger_session_summary`, `_trigger_session_summary_on_finish`, `_trigger_project_session_summaries`, `_resolve_finished_session`, `_auto_push_on_finish`, and `_build_continue_seed`.\n- The R&D dashboard render path builds project tiles and rows via `render_status_line_html`, `_project_summary_text`, `_project_status_dot`, `_project_activity_reflection`/`_render_activity_reflection_html`, `render_project_tile_html`, folder-group renderers, and `render_projects_view_html`, reading caches/registry only (no synchronous model calls).\n- Session/effort gathering for the project board is handled by `_gather_project_efforts`, `_render_effort_card`, `_registry_session_view`, `_merge_registry_sessions`, and `_gather_project_sessions`, bridging live `session_registry` sessions with effort-history sessions (deduped by session id) into the lane columns.\n\nNote: this is a structural summary grounded in the source; `anchor_gui.py` is a deliverable (the running application), not a typical produced trio document, so there is no separate goal/decisions/findings narrative to extract beyond its code structure."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1693,"cache_read_input_tokens":98615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1693},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1278bb0-8b81-4c5e-8dcf-7d023ebc7034","uuid":"7363789f-67f3-41d2-963d-288718c1d11a","request_id":"req_011CcJo4PPrb71Pb6YdjF4bh"}
